// Analytics build configuration — COMMITTED, and credential-free by design.
//
// Every value below is empty on purpose. A contributor clone, a fork and CI all build with
// empty analytics credentials, `AppInfo.telemetryDeckAppID` resolves to nil, and the analytics
// client no-ops entirely — so no build other than the owner's release machine can reach the
// owner's dataset. Keeping the dataset clean is the whole point; the app ID is a write-only
// ingestion key and is not a secret in any case.
//
// The release machine supplies the real values in `Config/Analytics.local.xcconfig`, which is
// gitignored and optionally included at the bottom of this file. Order matters — a later
// assignment wins, so the empty defaults must come first and the optional include last.

// TelemetryDeck's write-only ingestion key. Absent here; supplied by the local override.
TELEMETRYDECK_APP_ID =

// The identifier salt. This value is write-once: changing it after a release re-derives every
// anonymized identifier, so every existing install looks new to the vendor and all retention
// and DAU/MAU history resets with no way to reconcile the two sides afterwards.
TELEMETRYDECK_SALT =

// Optional include — the trailing `?` makes an absent file a silent no-op rather than an error,
// which is what lets a clean clone build without a configuration-file warning.
#include? "Analytics.local.xcconfig"
